      "text": "Let's denote the cost of a pen by \\( p \\) dollars and the cost of a pencil by \\( c \\) dollars. We have the following system of equations based on the problem statement:\n\n1. \\( 4p + 3c = 2.24 \\)\n2. \\( 2p + 5c = 1.54 \\)\n\nFirst, we will eliminate one of the variables. To do this, we can multiply the first equation by 2 and the second equation by 4 to make the coefficients of \\( p \\) the same:\n\n1. \\( 8p + 6c = 4.48 \\)\n2. \\( 8p + 20c = 6.16 \\)\n\nNext, we subtract the first equation from the second equation to eliminate \\( p \\):\n\n\\[\n(8p + 20c) - (8p + 6c) = 6.16 - 4.48\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n14c = 1.68\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( c \\):\n\n\\[\nc = \\frac{1.68}{14} = 0.12\n\\]\n\nSo, the cost of a pencil is \\( 0.12 \\) dollars. To express this in cents, we multiply by 100:\n\n\\[\n0.12 \\times 100 = 12\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of a pencil is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cents.",
