      "text": "Given the problem:\n\\[ 4p + 3c = 2.24 \\]\n\\[ 2p + 5c = 1.54 \\]\n\nFirst, solve for \\( p \\) and \\( c \\) in terms of one another. Let's start by solving the second equation for \\( p \\):\n\n\\[ 2p + 5c = 1.54 \\]\n\\[ 2p = 1.54 - 5c \\]\n\\[ p = \\frac{1.54 - 5c}{2} \\]\n\nNext, substitute this expression for \\( p \\) into the first equation:\n\n\\[ 4\\left(\\frac{1.54 - 5c}{2}\\right) + 3c = 2.24 \\]\n\\[ 2(1.54 - 5c) + 3c = 2.24 \\]\n\\[ 3.08 - 10c + 3c = 2.24 \\]\n\\[ 3.08 - 7c = 2.24 \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( c \\):\n\n\\[ 3.08 - 2.24 = 7c \\]\n\\[ 0.84 = 7c \\]\n\\[ c = \\frac{0.84}{7} \\]\n\\[ c = 0.12 \\]\n\nThus, the cost of a pencil is \\(\\boxed{12}\\) cents.",
